# Frontend Engineering

- Follow existing Quasar/Vue component, routing, state-management, and styling patterns
- Keep components focused and readable
- Move reusable logic into existing composables/hooks/utilities only when reuse is clear
- Use typed props, emits, state, API responses, and form models; do not mutate props directly
- Preserve existing UX unless the task asks for a change

Handle every relevant state: loading, disabled, validation errors, API failures, empty results, permission restrictions, responsive layout.

## Performance

- Avoid unnecessary re-renders and heavy computed logic on large datasets
- Debounce or throttle high-frequency operations when needed

## Accessibility basics

- Meaningful labels; keyboard-friendly controls; visible focus states
- Readable contrast; status never communicated by color alone
